From 4d05507ecaf05313ac7ac88892e12be768b421a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:36:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - remove algorithm alignment masks

The AES skciphers advertise a 16-byte Crypto API alignment requirement,
although the driver already validates DMA scatterlists and bounces those
that fail its hardware or cache-line checks. Keys and IVs are copied into
private storage, and aes_expandkey() accepts unaligned input.

Drop the nonzero AES skcipher masks and redundant zero initializers in
the other skcipher and AEAD registrations. The implicit zero mask avoids
imposing an additional caller alignment requirement. Keep the driver's
DMA alignment checks and bounce handling unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
---
 eip93-aead.c   | 16 ----------------
 eip93-cipher.c |  8 --------
 2 files changed, 24 deletions(-)

